---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy template for Che Xu Studio covering forms, checkout, analytics, and AI chat."
  path="/privacy"
  noindex={!siteConfig.allowIndexing}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-shell max-w-3xl prose-legal">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }]} />
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-navy-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-950">
        <strong>Owner / legal review required before launch.</strong> This template describes the data flows implemented in this website. It is not legal advice and does not guarantee compliance.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted sm:text-base">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Who we are</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            This website is operated by {siteConfig.legalName}. Contact details published on the Contact page (when configured) are the primary channel for privacy questions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Information we collect</h2>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong>Contact / lead forms:</strong> name, email, service interest, message, optional phone, optional project brief fields, marketing consent status, and timestamps.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Checkout:</strong> name, email, optional company/website/goal, and Stripe-handled payment details (card data never touches our servers).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Security signals:</strong> Cloudflare Turnstile tokens, IP-based rate-limit keys, and standard request metadata for abuse prevention.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>AI chat:</strong> messages you send during a session are processed to generate replies. Chat transcripts are not stored by default in our database.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Analytics (optional):</strong> privacy-conscious funnel events and/or Cloudflare Web Analytics page views when configured—without names, emails, messages, or payment data.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">How we use information</h2>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>Respond to enquiries and prepare quotes</li>
            <li>Create Stripe Checkout sessions and fulfil verified orders</li>
            <li>Provide AI assistant answers based on published site content</li>
            <li>Prevent spam and abuse</li>
            <li>Send marketing updates only when you give separate marketing consent</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Processors</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Depending on configuration, we use Cloudflare (hosting, D1, Workers AI, Turnstile, optional Web Analytics) and Stripe (payments). Their processing is subject to their respective terms and privacy policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Consented lead records and verified order records are stored in Cloudflare D1 for business operations and accounting needs. Exact retention periods should be set by the business owner and documented here before launch.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Your choices</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You may request access or correction of personal information we hold, withdraw marketing consent, or ask questions about this policy by contacting us through the Contact page.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Updates</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">We may update this policy as the website’s features or legal requirements change. Material updates should be reviewed before publication.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
